| `scp`         | Copies files between systems over SSH.                 | `scp file.txt user@192.168.1.10:/home/user/` |
| `traceroute`  | Shows the network path to a destination, if installed. | `traceroute google.com`                      |

## 9. Package Management Commands

For Debian-based Linux distributions such as Ubuntu and Raspberry Pi OS:

| Command            | Description                                           | Example                       |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `sudo apt update`  | Updates package repository information.               | `sudo apt update`             |
| `sudo apt upgrade` | Installs available package upgrades.                  | `sudo apt upgrade`            |
| `sudo apt install` | Installs a software package.                          | `sudo apt install gcc`        |
| `sudo apt remove`  | Removes an installed package.                         | `sudo apt remove gcc`         |
| `sudo apt purge`   | Removes a package and its system configuration files. | `sudo apt purge package-name` |
| `apt search`       | Searches available packages.                          | `apt search python3`          |
| `apt show`         | Displays package details.                             | `apt show gcc`                |
| `dpkg -l`          | Lists installed packages.                             | `dpkg -l`                     |

`sudo` runs a command with elevated privileges when the user is authorized to do so.

## 10. Searching Commands

| Command   | Description                                    | Example              |
| --------- | ---------------------------------------------- | -------------------- |
| `find`    | Searches for files and directories.            | `find . -name "*.c"` |
| `locate`  | Searches a filename database, if installed.    | `locate main.c`      |
| `which`   | Displays the executable path of a command.     | `which gcc`          |
| `whereis` | Locates binary, source, and manual files.      | `whereis gcc`        |
| `grep -r` | Searches text recursively through directories. | `grep -r "main" .`   |

## 11. Input, Output and Redirection Commands

| Command | Description                                    | Example                            |
| ------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| `echo`  | Prints text to the terminal.                   | `echo "Hello Linux"`               |
| `>`     | Redirects output and overwrites a file.        | `echo "Hello" > a.txt`             |
| `>>`    | Appends output to a file.                      | `echo "World" >> a.txt`            |
| `<`     | Uses a file as command input.                  | `sort < names.txt`                 |
| `\\|`   | Sends one command's output to another command. | `ls \\| grep ".c"`                 |
| `tee`   | Writes output to a file and displays it.       | `ls \\| tee files.txt`             |
| `xargs` | Builds command arguments from standard input.  | `printf "a.txt\n" \\| xargs ls -l` |

## 12. Archive and Compression Commands

| Command     | Description                             | Example                            |
| ----------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| `tar -cvf`  | Creates a tar archive.                  | `tar -cvf backup.tar project/`     |
| `tar -xvf`  | Extracts a tar archive.                 | `tar -xvf backup.tar`              |
| `tar -czvf` | Creates a gzip-compressed tar archive.  | `tar -czvf backup.tar.gz project/` |
| `tar -xzvf` | Extracts a gzip-compressed tar archive. | `tar -xzvf backup.tar.gz`          |
| `gzip`      | Compresses a file.                      | `gzip file.txt`                    |
| `gunzip`    | Decompresses a gzip file.               | `gunzip file.txt.gz`               |
| `zip`       | Creates a ZIP archive, if installed.    | `zip backup.zip file.txt`          |
| `unzip`     | Extracts a ZIP archive.                 | `unzip backup.zip`                 |

## 13. Linux Commands for Embedded Systems and Raspberry Pi

| Command              | Description                                                                                      | Example                     |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------- |
| `gcc`                | Compiles C programs.                                                                             | `gcc main.c -o main`        |
| `./main`             | Executes a compiled program in the current directory.                                            | `./main`                    |
| `make`               | Builds software using a Makefile.                                                                | `make`                      |
| `ls /dev`            | Lists device files.                                                                              | `ls /dev`                   |
| `ls /dev/tty*`       | Lists device paths matching the serial-terminal naming pattern.                                  | `ls /dev/tty*`              |
| `ls /sys/class/gpio` | Checks for the legacy GPIO sysfs interface.                                                      | `ls /sys/class/gpio`        |
| `ls /dev/gpiochip*`  | Lists GPIO character devices, if present.                                                        | `ls /dev/gpiochip*`         |
| `journalctl -b`      | Displays system journal logs from the current boot.                                              | `journalctl -b`             |
| `systemctl status`   | Displays the status of a specified system service.                                               | `systemctl status ssh`      |
| `systemctl start`    | Starts a system service.                                                                         | `sudo systemctl start ssh`  |
| `systemctl stop`     | Stops a system service.                                                                          | `sudo systemctl stop ssh`   |
| `systemctl enable`   | Configures a service to start automatically at boot.                                             | `sudo systemctl enable ssh` |
| `i2cdetect -y 1`     | Scans I²C bus 1 for responding addresses, if the I²C tools are installed and the bus is enabled. | `sudo i2cdetect -y 1`       |
| `lsmod`              | Lists loaded kernel modules.                                                                     | `lsmod`                     |
| `modinfo`            | Displays information about a kernel module.                                                      | `modinfo module_name`       |

Some commands depend on the Linux distribution, installed utilities, hardware, and permissions. Raspberry Pi GPIO and I²C device paths can also differ by OS version and configuration.

## 14. Shutdown and Restart Commands

| Command          | Description                            | Example               |
| ---------------- | -------------------------------------- | --------------------- |
| `shutdown now`   | Shuts down the system immediately.     | `sudo shutdown now`   |
| `shutdown -h +5` | Schedules shutdown after five minutes. | `sudo shutdown -h +5` |
| `shutdown -c`    | Cancels a scheduled shutdown.          | `sudo shutdown -c`    |
| `reboot`         | Restarts the system.                   | `sudo reboot`         |
| `poweroff`       | Powers off the system.                 | `sudo poweroff`       |

Save your work before shutting down or restarting.

